@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] antithesis-proof-boundaries
Harness-only adapters MUST identify controlled, emulated and native effects separately. A successful adapter response MUST NOT establish a physical effect that its independent oracle has not observed. Unknown or unavailable observations MUST NOT be interpreted as absence, success or expected refusal.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] antithesis-runtime-secret-custody
Runtime credentials, keys, tokens and user payloads MUST NOT enter images, source manifests or diagnostics. Synthetic credentials MUST be generated or installed into private runtime state and passed through the reviewed service interfaces.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] antithesis-immutable-run-identity
Every submitted configuration MUST bind its source selection, dependencies, executable artifacts, image digests, test commands and assertion roster to an immutable manifest. A passing result MUST retain that identity and its actual execution scope.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] antithesis-setup-owner
Exactly one workload bootstrap owner MUST signal setup completion after the selected services, fixture identities and independent oracles are ready. Test commands MUST NOT signal setup completion. Failed prerequisites MUST leave setup incomplete.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity;verification] antithesis-stub-storage-substrate
The `admission-stub` storage substrate is a harness-only stub, not ZFS: its pool totals are configured, its image is non-bootable, and it is selected only by explicit Compose environment on the controlled Lilly release. Stub-backed runs MUST NOT claim native ZFS, physical capacity, KVM, Firecracker or isolation, and MUST NOT fake admission results; admission decisions MUST run through real Marshall actions and be witnessed in PostgreSQL. Its explicit stub-delete opt-in MAY settle a delete only with the deleted facts for a placement the controlled executor observably never created anything for, never for a placement that ran.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;verification] antithesis-labelled-stand-ins
A harness stand-in for a missing substrate, such as the guest stand-in in `config/compose.satellite-standin.yaml`, MUST be named as a stand-in in its overlay, source, profile documentation and property notes. It MUST NOT receive VM, placement, execution or credential authority, and its assertions MUST claim only the behaviour of the real services it exercises, never guest, tap, isolation or native effects.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification;capacity] antithesis-stub-substrate-labelled
A stubbed native substrate, such as the guest-lifecycle profile's synthetic storage pool, MUST be named a stub in its code, Compose overlay, selection notes and README. It MUST grant only the bounded synthetic capacity needed to admit the selected emulated workload, and assertions over it MUST NOT claim native ZFS, KVM, Firecracker or isolation properties.
